    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1338">

                <pb facs="1207" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg949"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador:</hi> Replying to your note
                    of to-day’s date in regard to an interview with Captain Boy-Ed for the purpose
                    of learning the reasons for the request for his recall, I regret to say that I
                    can only discuss the matter with you, and am unwilling to have an interview on
                    the subject with Captain Boy-Ed. In view of the action already taken, I can see
                    no good purpose in further discussion, as the decision of this Government was
                    reached only after long and careful consideration.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
